{
 "_comment": [
  "Hand-authored marker KEYFRAMES for the 360 spin set.",
  "",
  "Eight keyframes, one per named view, evenly spaced around the turn:",
  "front - front-left - left - rear-left - rear - rear-right - right - front-right.",
  "build-hotspots.py interpolates these around the ring to whatever frame count",
  "the spin set actually has, so going from 16 to 48 frames costs nothing here.",
  "",
  "space = 'bbox': coordinates are a fraction of THE PRODUCT'S OWN BOUNDS in",
  "that frame, x 0=left 1=right, y 0=top 1=bottom. Deliberately not a fraction",
  "of the frame: re-packing the set would then silently move every marker off",
  "the part it names. Against the product's own box they are invariant.",
  "",
  "null = not visible from that view. A marker is drawn only where BOTH",
  "surrounding keyframes agree it is visible, so it fades out of the turn at a",
  "sensible place instead of blinking.",
  "",
  "Positions were read off a 10% coordinate grid laid over each named view.",
  "Re-run tools/build-hotspots.py after editing."
 ],
